IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uro-nouns`

-- Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2026 (S.I. 2026/148): PART 2, ARTICLES 3 TO 6.
-- Layer 1. Article 3 sends the reader to Schedule 1 (module uro-schedule1-contributions-act-rates).
-- Articles 4 to 6 state some figures outright ("for 135.50 substitute 140.65") and, for other sums, only a
-- percentage ("shall be increased by 3.8 per cent"). A percentage rule is a function of the sum the parent
-- instrument carries before the Order; that sum is not in the text, so it is a plain input, and the rule
-- returns the exact product. The Order states no rounding rule (NOTES.md, fork F-01).
-- The dates on which these changes take effect are article 7 (uro-part2-effect-dates).

§ `Article 3 -- Rates or amounts of certain benefits under the Contributions and Benefits Act`

-- art 3 sorts every sum of Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act into: raised to the Schedule 1
-- figure; left out of the increase; or not mentioned at all (a sum in Part II is not one of the Parts the
-- article names).
-- src:63 | 3 Rates or amounts of certain benefits under the Contributions and Benefits Act
-- src:64 | (1) The sums specified in paragraph (2) shall be increased so that Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act (contributory periodical benefits, non-contributory periodical benefits, increases for dependants and rates of industrial injuries benefit), except paragraph 5 of Part III of that Schedule (guardian’s allowance), has effect as set out in Schedule 1 to this Order.
-- src:65 | (2) The sums mentioned in paragraph (1) are the sums specified in Parts I, III, IV and V of Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act except in—
-- src:66 | (a) Part III, the sum specified for age addition to a pension of any category, and otherwise under section 79 of that Act; and
-- src:67 | (b) Part V, the sums specified for the increase in disablement pension for dependent children and death benefit allowance in respect of children and qualifying young persons.
@ref art 3 (src:63-67)
DECLARE `a sum in Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act` IS ONE OF
    `a sum in Part I of Schedule 4`
    `a sum in Part III of Schedule 4 other than age addition and guardian's allowance`
    `age addition in Part III of Schedule 4 (to a pension of any category, and otherwise under section 79)`
    `guardian's allowance, paragraph 5 of Part III of Schedule 4`
    `a sum in Part IV of Schedule 4`
    `a sum in Part V of Schedule 4 other than the child increase and the child allowance`
    `the increase in disablement pension for dependent children (Part V of Schedule 4)`
    `death benefit allowance in respect of children and qualifying young persons (Part V of Schedule 4)`
    `a sum in a Part of Schedule 4 not named in art 3(2)`

@ref art 3 (src:63-67)
DECLARE `what art 3 does to a sum in Schedule 4` IS ONE OF
    `increased: Schedule 4 has effect as set out in Schedule 1`
    `excepted from the increase by art 3`
    `not mentioned in art 3`

@ref art 3(1), (2) (src:63-67)
GIVEN `the sum` IS A `a sum in Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act`
GIVETH A `what art 3 does to a sum in Schedule 4`
`art 3: what the article does to the sum` `the sum` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sum`
    WHEN `a sum in Part I of Schedule 4` THEN `increased: Schedule 4 has effect as set out in Schedule 1`
    WHEN `a sum in Part III of Schedule 4 other than age addition and guardian's allowance` THEN `increased: Schedule 4 has effect as set out in Schedule 1`
    WHEN `age addition in Part III of Schedule 4 (to a pension of any category, and otherwise under section 79)` THEN `excepted from the increase by art 3`
    WHEN `guardian's allowance, paragraph 5 of Part III of Schedule 4` THEN `excepted from the increase by art 3`
    WHEN `a sum in Part IV of Schedule 4` THEN `increased: Schedule 4 has effect as set out in Schedule 1`
    WHEN `a sum in Part V of Schedule 4 other than the child increase and the child allowance` THEN `increased: Schedule 4 has effect as set out in Schedule 1`
    WHEN `the increase in disablement pension for dependent children (Part V of Schedule 4)` THEN `excepted from the increase by art 3`
    WHEN `death benefit allowance in respect of children and qualifying young persons (Part V of Schedule 4)` THEN `excepted from the increase by art 3`
    WHEN `a sum in a Part of Schedule 4 not named in art 3(2)` THEN `not mentioned in art 3`

§ `Article 4 -- Increase in rates or amounts of certain pensions and allowances under the Contributions and Benefits Act`

§§ `Article 4(1)`

-- out of text: Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 Sch 7 para 13(4) (the sums calculated for a beneficiary's retirement allowance)
-- src:69 | (1) The sums falling to be calculated under paragraph 13(4) of Schedule 7 to the Contributions and Benefits Act (calculation of weekly rate of a beneficiary’s retirement allowance) shall be increased by 3.8 per cent.
@ref art 4(1) (src:69)
GIVEN `the sum calculated under paragraph 13(4) of Schedule 7` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 4(1): the retirement allowance sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the sum calculated under paragraph 13(4) of Schedule 7` MEANS
    `the sum calculated under paragraph 13(4) of Schedule 7` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)

§§ `Article 4(2) -- section 44(4) of the Contributions and Benefits Act`

-- src:70 | (2) In section 44(4) of the Contributions and Benefits Act (basic pension in a Category A retirement pension)—
-- src:71 | (a) for “£135.50” substitute “£140.65”; and
@ref art 4(2)(a) (src:70-71)
`art 4(2)(a): section 44(4) sum replaced in paragraph (a)` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 135.50, 140.65

-- src:72 | (b) for “£176.45” substitute “£184.90”.
@ref art 4(2)(b) (src:72)
`art 4(2)(b): section 44(4) sum replaced in paragraph (b)` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 176.45, 184.90

@ref art 4(2) (src:70-72)
DECLARE `a sum in section 44(4) of the Contributions and Benefits Act that art 4(2) replaces` IS ONE OF
    `section 44(4) sum replaced in art 4(2)(a)`
    `section 44(4) sum replaced in art 4(2)(b)`

@ref art 4(2) (src:70-72)
GIVEN `which one` IS A `a sum in section 44(4) of the Contributions and Benefits Act that art 4(2) replaces`
GIVETH A `a sum and its replacement`
`art 4(2): the replaced and the replacing sum` `which one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which one`
    WHEN `section 44(4) sum replaced in art 4(2)(a)` THEN `art 4(2)(a): section 44(4) sum replaced in paragraph (a)`
    WHEN `section 44(4) sum replaced in art 4(2)(b)` THEN `art 4(2)(b): section 44(4) sum replaced in paragraph (b)`


§§ `Article 4(3) -- sums directed to be increased by 3.8 per cent`

-- out of text: Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (additional pension; 'final relevant year'): the sum before the Order and the first calendar year of the final relevant year are inputs.
-- "It is directed that the sums which are ... shall in each case be increased by 3.8 per cent." (a) bites
-- only on a sum "calculated by reference to any final relevant year earlier than the tax year 2025-2026":
-- the year is the first calendar year of the final relevant year (2024 for 2024-25); a later one: NOTHING.
-- src:73 | (3) It is directed that the sums which are—
-- src:74 | (a) additional pensions in long-term benefits calculated by reference to any final relevant year earlier than the tax year 2025-2026;
-- src:78 | shall in each case be increased by 3.8 per cent.
@ref art 4(3)(a) (src:73-78)
GIVEN `the first calendar year of the final relevant year` IS A NUMBER
      `the additional pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`art 4(3)(a): the additional pension after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the first calendar year of the final relevant year` `the additional pension` MEANS
    IF `the first calendar year of the final relevant year` LESS THAN 2025
    THEN JUST (`the additional pension` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- out of text: Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 Sch 5 (increase of retirement pension where entitlement is deferred): the sum before the Order is an input.
-- src:73 | (3) It is directed that the sums which are—
-- src:75 | (b) increases in the rates of retirement pensions under Schedule 5 to the Contributions and Benefits Act (pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to retirement pension is deferred);
-- src:78 | shall in each case be increased by 3.8 per cent.
@ref art 4(3)(b) (src:73-78)
GIVEN `the increase in the rate of a retirement pension under Schedule 5 (entitlement deferred)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 4(3)(b): the Schedule 5 increase after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the increase in the rate of a retirement pension under Schedule 5 (entitlement deferred)` MEANS
    `the increase in the rate of a retirement pension under Schedule 5 (entitlement deferred)` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)

-- out of text: Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 Sch 5 para 7A (lump sum): the sum before the Order is an input.
-- src:73 | (3) It is directed that the sums which are—
-- src:76 | (c) lump sums to which surviving spouses or civil partners will become entitled under paragraph 7A of that Schedule on becoming entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension (entitlement to lump sum where pensioner’s deceased spouse or civil partner has deferred entitlement); and
-- src:78 | shall in each case be increased by 3.8 per cent.
@ref art 4(3)(c) (src:73-78)
GIVEN `the lump sum under paragraph 7A of Schedule 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 4(3)(c): the paragraph 7A lump sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the lump sum under paragraph 7A of Schedule 5` MEANS
    `the lump sum under paragraph 7A of Schedule 5` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)

-- out of text: Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 ss 126A, 63 and 150 (order-made sums): the sum before the Order is an input.
-- src:73 | (3) It is directed that the sums which are—
-- src:77 | (d) sums payable to a pensioner as part of their Category A or Category B retirement pension by virtue of an order made under section 126A of the Social Security Act 1975, section 63 of the Social Security Act 1986 or section 150 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 by virtue of subsection (1)(e),
-- src:78 | shall in each case be increased by 3.8 per cent.
@ref art 4(3)(d) (src:73-78)
GIVEN `the sum payable as part of a Category A or B retirement pension by virtue of an order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 4(3)(d): the sum payable by virtue of an order after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the sum payable as part of a Category A or B retirement pension by virtue of an order` MEANS
    `the sum payable as part of a Category A or B retirement pension by virtue of an order` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)

DECLARE `a sum that art 4(3) directs to be increased` IS ONE OF
    `an additional pension calculated by reference to a final relevant year before 2025-26`
    `an increase in the rate of a retirement pension where entitlement is deferred (Schedule 5)`
    `a lump sum for a surviving spouse or civil partner (paragraph 7A of Schedule 5)`
    `a sum payable as part of a Category A or B retirement pension by virtue of an order under section 126A, 63 or 150`
    `a sum not described in art 4(3)`

-- out of text: Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (the places art 4(3) lists): the sum before the Order and the first calendar year of the final relevant year are inputs.
@ref art 4(3) (src:73-78)
GIVEN `which sum` IS A `a sum that art 4(3) directs to be increased`
      `the first calendar year of the final relevant year` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum before the increase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`art 4(3): the sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `which sum` `the first calendar year of the final relevant year` `the sum before the increase` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which sum`
    WHEN `an additional pension calculated by reference to a final relevant year before 2025-26` THEN `art 4(3)(a): the additional pension after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the first calendar year of the final relevant year` `the sum before the increase`
    WHEN `an increase in the rate of a retirement pension where entitlement is deferred (Schedule 5)` THEN JUST (`art 4(3)(b): the Schedule 5 increase after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the sum before the increase`)
    WHEN `a lump sum for a surviving spouse or civil partner (paragraph 7A of Schedule 5)` THEN JUST (`art 4(3)(c): the paragraph 7A lump sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the sum before the increase`)
    WHEN `a sum payable as part of a Category A or B retirement pension by virtue of an order under section 126A, 63 or 150` THEN JUST (`art 4(3)(d): the sum payable by virtue of an order after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the sum before the increase`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Article 4(4) -- shared additional pensions`

