GIVEN `the shared additional pension under section 55A or 55AA` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 4(4)(a): the shared additional pension after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the shared additional pension under section 55A or 55AA` MEANS
    `the shared additional pension under section 55A or 55AA` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)

-- out of text: Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 Sch 5A para 2: the sum before the Order is an input.
-- src:79 | (4) The sums which, under—
-- src:81 | (b) paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A to the Contributions and Benefits Act, are increases in the rates of such pensions,
-- src:82 | shall in each case be increased by 3.8 per cent.
@ref art 4(4)(b) (src:79-82)
GIVEN `the increase in a shared additional pension under paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`art 4(4)(b): the paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A increase after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the increase in a shared additional pension under paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A` MEANS
    `the increase in a shared additional pension under paragraph 2 of Schedule 5A` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)

§ `Article 5 -- Increase in rates or amount of certain benefits under the Pension Schemes Act`

-- out of text: Pension Schemes Act 1993 s 15(1) and the tax year of the earnings factors: the sum payable and the first calendar year of that tax year are inputs.
-- The tax year of the earnings factors is its first calendar year (1987 for 1987-88). 1987-88 and earlier:
-- 3.8 per cent. 1988-89 to 1996-97 inclusive: 0.8 per cent. Any later year: the Order says nothing: NOTHING.
-- src:83 | 5 Increase in rates or amount of certain benefits under the Pension Schemes Act
-- src:84 | It is directed that the sums which are payable by virtue of section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (increase of guaranteed minimum where commencement of guaranteed minimum pension postponed) to a person who is also entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension (including sums payable by virtue of section 17(2) and (3) of that Act) shall be increased by—
-- src:85 | (a) 3.8 per cent where the increase under section 15(1) is attributable to earnings factors for the tax year 1987-88 and earlier tax years; and
@ref art 5(a) (src:83-85)
GIVEN `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`art 5(a): the guaranteed minimum increase after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` `the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act` MEANS
    IF `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` AT MOST 1987
    THEN JUST (`the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act` TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- out of text: Pension Schemes Act 1993 s 15(1) and the tax year of the earnings factors: the sum payable and the first calendar year of that tax year are inputs.
-- src:84 | It is directed that the sums which are payable by virtue of section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act (increase of guaranteed minimum where commencement of guaranteed minimum pension postponed) to a person who is also entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension (including sums payable by virtue of section 17(2) and (3) of that Act) shall be increased by—
-- src:86 | (b) 0.8 per cent where the increase under section 15(1) is attributable to earnings factors for the tax years 1988-89 to 1996-97 inclusive.
@ref art 5(b) (src:84-86)
GIVEN `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`art 5(b): the guaranteed minimum increase after the increase of 0.8 per cent` `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` `the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act` MEANS
    IF `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` AT LEAST 1988 AND `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` AT MOST 1996
    THEN JUST (`the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act` TIMES (1 PLUS 0.8%))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- out of text: Pension Schemes Act 1993 s 15(1) and the tax year of the earnings factors: the sum payable and the first calendar year of that tax year are inputs.
@ref art 5 (src:83-86)
GIVEN `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`art 5: the guaranteed minimum increase after the increase` `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` `the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` AT MOST 1987
           THEN `art 5(a): the guaranteed minimum increase after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` `the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act`
           OTHERWISE `art 5(b): the guaranteed minimum increase after the increase of 0.8 per cent` `the first calendar year of the tax year of the earnings factors` `the sum payable under section 15(1) of the Pension Schemes Act`

§ `Article 6 -- Increase in rates or amounts of certain pensions under Part 1 of the Pensions Act`

